pine is believed to work by blocking a number of receptors, including those for serotonin and dopamine.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"Quetiapine","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quetiapine","acts":[{"how":"antagonist","on":["5-HT2A receptor","Dopamine D2 receptor","Histamine H1 receptor"]},{"how":"agonist","on":["5-HT1A receptor"]}],"guide":50,"kind":"Atypical antipsychotic","body":[{"what":"halfLife","says":"7 hours (parent compound); 9–12 hours (active metabolite, norquetiapine)"},{"what":"brokenDown","says":"Liver via CYP3A4-catalysed sulfoxidation to its active metabolite norquetiapine (N-desalkylquetiapine)"},{"what":"leaves","says":"Kidney (73%), feces (20%)"}],"figures":"Quetiapine"},"uses":{"text":"Quetiapine, sold under the brand name Seroquel among others, is a medication of the atypical antipsychotic class. It is used in the treatment of schizophrenia, bipolar disorder, and major depressive disorder. Quetiapine is also widely prescribed off-label as a sleep aid for its tranquillizing effects.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"Quetiapine","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quetiapine","brands":"Seroquel, Seroquel Xr","routes":"By mouth","figures":"Quetiapine"},"sideEffects":{"text":"Common side effects include sedation, fatigue, weight gain, constipation, and dry mouth.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"Quetiapine","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quetiapine"},"zh":"喹硫平","summaryZh":"喹硫平），以Seroquel（思樂康）等品牌名稱於市場上銷售，是一種非典型抗精神病藥物，用於治療思覺失調症、雙相障礙（躁鬱症）以及嚴重憂鬱疾患（重度憂鬱症）。由於其具有鎮靜效果，而被廣泛作為安眠藥處方使用，但這類用途的益處可能無法抵銷其不良副作用的風險。此藥物採口服方式給藥。"}